  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Language tags (xml:lang) on literals in the RELS-EXT datastream are ignored by the triple store. For example:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<rdf:Description xmlns:skos=\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\" rdf:about=\"info:fedora/aat:300006036\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<skos:prefLabel xml:lang=\"nl-NL\">postkantoren</skos:prefLabel>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "....",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "SPARQL queries only retrieve the literal \"postkantoren\" without the language tag.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "In contrast, triples from the DC datastream do retain the language information correctly. So this is not a pure triple store issue but an issue of translating RELS-EXT into triples (and maybe also RELS-INT, but I did not check that).",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "If this issue is resolved, it would also be nice if the REST API methods for adding/deleting Relationships would be extended with a language parameter.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
