  "description": "<p>Language tags (xml:lang) on literals in the RELS-EXT datastream are ignored by the triple store. For example:<br/>\n&lt;rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;rdf:Description xmlns:skos=\"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#\" rdf:about=\"info:fedora/aat:300006036\"&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;skos:prefLabel xml:lang=\"nl-NL\"&gt;postkantoren&lt;/skos:prefLabel&gt;<br/>\n    ....<br/>\nSPARQL queries only retrieve the literal \"postkantoren\" without the language tag.<br/>\nIn contrast, triples from the DC datastream do retain the language information correctly. So this is not a pure triple store issue but an issue of translating RELS-EXT into triples (and maybe also RELS-INT, but I did not check that).<br/>\nIf this issue is resolved, it would also be nice if the REST API methods for adding/deleting Relationships would be extended with a language parameter.</p>",
